# Project Overview

EnterpriseStarter is a Vue 3 + .NET modular monolith. Aspire is the default development entry point; Compose is a reference deployment.

## Layout

```
├── apps/web/                 # Vue SPA; cookie/CSRF fetch client
├── apps/api/                 # Thin executable host
├── apps/platform/            # Identity, RBAC, data, audit, migrations
├── apps/module-abstractions/ # Compile-time module contract and registry
├── apps/api.tests/           # API integration tests
├── aspire/
│   ├── AppHost/       # Dev orchestration (not production)
│   └── ServiceDefaults/
├── e2e/               # Playwright
├── docker-compose.yml # Optional deploy
└── EnterpriseStarter.sln
```

## Stack

| Layer | Tech |
|-------|------|
| Frontend | Vue 3, Pinia, Vue Router, Tailwind 4, template library `@/ui` (primitives + chrome), `fetch`; production PWA of the same SPA |
| Backend | .NET 10 host + platform + module abstractions |
| AuthN | Identity HttpOnly cookie and CSRF header |
| AuthZ | Global roles with code-defined permission claims |
| API | `/api/v1` |
| Data | PostgreSQL-only shared `EnterpriseDbContext` migration stream |
| Modules | Explicit compile-time registration; production registry empty |
| Orchestration | Aspire (dev); Compose migrator + api + nginx (deploy) |
| Tests | Vitest (web), xUnit (api), Playwright (e2e) |

## Auth

- Session: `enterprise_starter_auth`; the SPA stores no bearer token.
- Authenticated mutations require `X-CSRF-TOKEN`.
- Permission policies protect users, roles, and security audit.
- Admins create users with temporary passwords; new users must change them.
- There is no public registration.

The baseline has no business modules, public registration, or multitenancy. OIDC, MFA, email, jobs, storage, and tenancy are product extensions.

## Dev workflow

```bash
# Preferred
dotnet run --project aspire/AppHost

# Or standalone (Postgres required)
dotnet run --project apps/api
cd apps/web && npm run dev   # VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api/v1
```

## Deploy (optional)

```bash
cp .env.docker.example .env   # POSTGRES_PASSWORD + SEED_ADMIN_PASSWORD
docker compose up --build     # http://localhost:8080
```

Not used for local dev. Skill: `run-docker-deploy`. Runbook: `.cursor/docs/DEPLOY-RUNBOOK.md`.

